  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN mystic slimes arranged in a line, and the power of the iii-th slime is AiA_iAi​.\n\nYou need to perform the following operations until only one slime remains:\n\n\nChoose two adjacent indices iii, jjj (1≤i,j≤∣A∣1 \\leq i, j \\leq |A|1≤i,j≤∣A∣, ∣i−j∣=1|i - j| = 1∣i−j∣=1), and let the iii-th slime eat the jjj-th slime. After this operation, the power of the iii-th slime becomes max⁡(0,Ai−Aj)\\max(0, A_i - A_j)max(0,Ai​−Aj​) (while the jjj-th slime is removed).\nHere, it is **not** necessary that Ai≥AjA_i \\ge A_jAi​≥Aj​, i.e. even a smaller slime can eat a bigger slime.\nNote that after each operation, the number of slimes decreases by 111, and all slimes are reindexed starting from 111. The relative order between uneaten slimes remains unchanged.\n\nFind the maximum possible power of the last remaining slime.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test contains NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible power of the last remaining slime.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\le T \\le 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤502 \\le N \\le 502≤N≤50",
      "1≤Ai≤10001 \\le A_i \\le 10001≤Ai​≤1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n2\n1 2\n3\n1 2 3\n3\n1 100 10\n2\n1000 1000\n4\n1 1 1 1",
        "output": "1\n3\n89\n0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : We choose indices i=2,j=1i = 2, j = 1i=2,j=1 and let 222nd slime eat the 111st. Now, the new power of the 222nd slime becomes 111 (and it is re-indexed to position 111). Since only one slime remains, the answer here is 111.\nTest Case 2 : We perform the following steps:\n\nA=[1,2,3]A = [1, 2, 3]A=[1,2,3], pick i=1,j=2i = 1, j = 2i=1,j=2. The updated powers are [0,3][0, 3][0,3].\nA=[0,3]A = [0, 3]A=[0,3], pick i=2,j=1i = 2, j = 1i=2,j=1. The updated power of the last remaining slime is 333.\n\nHence, the answer is 333."
      }
    ]
